{
  "dom_id": "step-q74941",
  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}3y+x \\\\ y-x\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}x+3y \\\\ -x+y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x+3y \\\\ -x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x+3y \\\\ -x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
